// General Layers
LAYER_GENERAL_01 (0) - General Dimensions & Grid
LAYER_GENERAL_02 (1) - Title Block & Scale
LAYER_GENERAL_03 (2) - Reference Lines & Dimensions

// Wall Layers
LAYER_WALL_01 (3) - Exterior Walls
LAYER_WALL_02 (4) - Interior Walls - Structural
LAYER_WALL_03 (5) - Interior Walls - Non-Structural
LAYER_WALL_04 (6) - Partitions - Acoustic (Meeting Rooms)

// Floor & Ceiling Layers
LAYER_FLOOR_01 (7) - Floor Slab
LAYER_CEILING_01 (8) - Ceiling Grid
LAYER_CEILING_02 (9) - Ceiling Tiles

// Furniture Layers
LAYER_WORKSTATION_01 (10) - Workstations
LAYER_MEETING_TABLE_01 (11) - Meeting Tables
LAYER_CHAIR_01 (12) - Chairs
LAYER_FURNITURE_SUPPORT_01 (13) - Furniture Supports (Legs, etc.)

// Electrical Layers
LAYER_ELECTRICAL_01 (14) - Conduit
LAYER_ELECTRICAL_02 (15) - Outlets & Switches
LAYER_ELECTRICAL_03 (16) - Lighting Fixtures

// Annotation Layers
LAYER_NOTES_01 (17) - General Notes
LAYER_NOTES_02 (18) - Detail Notes
LAYER_TEXT_01 (19) - Text Labels

// Layout Specifications:

// Building Dimensions: 100ft x 50ft
// Occupancy Type: Business Assembly (NFPA 101 Compliance)
// Max Travel Distance: 75ft

// Zones:
// 1. Workstations (Approx. 3,000 sq. ft.) - Arranged in rows, spaced for circulation.
// 2. Meeting Rooms (2 x 500 sq. ft.) - Located near the center.
// 3. Break Area (Approx. 500 sq. ft.) - Adjacent to one of the meeting rooms.

// Workstation Layout:
// - Workstations: 5ft x 5ft
// - Row Spacing: 3ft between workstations
// - Total Workstation Area: 3,000 sq. ft. / 25 sq. ft. per workstation = 120 workstations
// - Arrangement:  Rows of 20 workstations each, running parallel to the 100ft wall.  Spacing between rows: 3ft.

// Meeting Room Layout:
// - Meeting Tables: 8ft x 4ft
// - Table Spacing: 6ft between tables
// - Room Dimensions: 20ft x 20ft (Each room)
// - Arrangement: Two rooms, each accommodating 5 tables.

// Break Area Layout:
// - Small table and chairs
// - Refrigerator and microwave (placed strategically)
// - Dimensions: 10ft x 10ft

// Electrical Outlets:
// - Workstations: 2 outlets per workstation (one on each side)
// - Meeting Rooms: 3 outlets per table
// - Break Area: 2 outlets

// NFPA 101 Compliance:
// - All exits (North & South Walls) must be within 75ft of any workstation.
// - Meeting rooms must be within 75ft of an exit.
// - Break area must be within 75ft of an exit.

// Layer Details:
// - WALL_01, WALL_02, WALL_03, WALL_04:  Use appropriate line weights and colors for different wall types.
// - FLOOR_01:  Solid color representing the floor slab.
// - CEILING_01, CEILING_02:  Grid lines and ceiling tile representation.
// - WORKSTATION_01:  Polylines representing the workstation outlines.
// - MEETING_TABLE_01:  Polylines representing the meeting table outlines.
// - ELECTRICAL_01:  Use appropriate conduit symbols and dimensions.
// - ELECTRICAL_02:  Place outlets and switches accurately, adhering to electrical code.
// - NOTES_01, NOTES_02, TEXT_01:  Use for general notes, detail notes, and text labels.

// CAD File Structure:
// - Create separate layers for each element (walls, floors, furniture, electrical).
// - Use layer locking and visibility settings to control the display of different elements.
// - Incorporate dimensioning and annotation to provide clear and concise information.
